{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "Studio API",
    "description": "Studio turns audio and video into transcriptions, translations, subtitles and dubbing. Use this API to create projects, order translation and dubbing, follow the progress, and download the results.\n\n## Authentication\nSend your Phrase Platform API token with every request, as `X-API-Key: <token>` or as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. A missing, invalid or expired token is answered with `401`. `403` means the token is valid but the action is not allowed: the item is someone else's, a share does not include the step or language, or your organization is blocked.\n\n## Typical flow\n1. Create a project with `POST /v1/projects`: upload files, or give direct links to media files. It answers with the project `id`. To add a recording to a project that exists, call `POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/recordings/upload-url`, upload the file to the url it returns, then call `POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/recordings`.\n2. Poll `GET /v1/projects/{projectId}/recordings/{recordingId}/status` until the transcription is `done`. Every long step answers `202` and runs in the background: you poll the status, you do not wait on the call.\n3. Optional: `POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/recordings/{recordingId}/estimates` tells what a translation costs before you start it.\n4. Order translation with `POST …/translate`, and wait until the status shows the language as `done`.\n5. Order dubbing with `POST …/dubbing`. A language must be translated before it can be dubbed, otherwise the call answers `400`.\n6. Read and download: `GET …/subtitles` for the text, the result endpoints for summary and insights, `POST …/exports` for a file, then `GET …/exports/{exportId}` until it is `done`.\n\n## Credits\nCredits are minutes. Transcription and every new translation language use `ceil(duration / 60)` minutes of the recording. Dubbing, retranscription and retranslation use none. The estimate endpoint tells the price in advance. When an organization has no credits left, starting work is refused with `403` (`No remaining minutes available`): creating a project, adding a recording, transcribe, translate and dubbing. Reading results, estimates and generating speech still work.\n\n## Errors\nErrors are JSON: `{ \"statusCode\": 400, \"message\": \"...\", \"timestamp\": \"...\" }`. The `message` says what to change.\n- `400` the request is invalid.\n- `401` the token is missing, invalid or expired.\n- `403` the token is valid but the action is not allowed.\n- `404` the item does not exist, is not visible to you, or you may not manage it. Items of other organizations always answer `404`.\n- `409` an item with that name already exists.\n- `429` too many requests; wait and try again.\n- `5xx` a failure on our side or at a provider; try again later.\n\n## Where the ids come from\nIds that Studio accepts but does not list belong to other Phrase products. `tmsProjectTemplateUid`, `termBases`, `mtProfileId` and `translationMemoryId` are Phrase TMS uids: get them from the Phrase TMS API (project templates, term bases, translation memories, machine translation profiles). `styleGuides` ids come from the Style Guides API. Both are described at https://developers.phrase.com/en/api/overview. Every other id (projects, recordings, glossaries, insights, pronunciations, templates, subtitle profiles, voices) comes from the list endpoints of this API.",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.studio.us.phrase.com",
      "description": "Production US Environment"
    },
    {
