      "description": "Production EU Environment"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Projects",
      "description": "Create, list, open, rename, archive, copy and delete projects. A project holds one or more recordings. Start here with `POST /v1/projects`."
    },
    {
      "name": "Recordings",
      "description": "The recordings of a project: add one, follow its status, order translation and dubbing, manage its speakers, delete it. Long steps answer `202`; poll `GET …/status` for the result."
    },
    {
      "name": "Subtitle Profiles",
      "description": "Subtitle layout rules (line length, reading speed and so on). Pick one per language when you create a project. Members of your organization can read them; the owner or a manager changes them."
    },
    {
      "name": "Fonts",
      "description": "The custom fonts of your organization, the same as the Custom Fonts settings of Studio: list, rename, delete and download them. Fonts are uploaded in Studio, where you confirm that you have the right to use them. Use the `fontFamily` value of a family (`custom:<id>`) in a subtitle profile to burn subtitles in that font."
    },
    {
      "name": "Pronunciations",
      "description": "Sets of words with the way to say them, used when text is turned into speech. Members of your organization can read them; the owner or a manager changes them."
    },
    {
      "name": "Glossaries",
      "description": "Terms and their translations, applied when a recording is translated. Members of your organization can read them; the owner or a manager changes them."
    },
    {
      "name": "Insights",
      "description": "Questions Studio answers about a recording, such as topics or action items. Members of your organization can read them; the owner or a manager changes them."
    },
    {
      "name": "Safe Communications",
      "description": "The safe communication checks Studio can run on a recording. List them here, then use their ids when you create a project."
    },
    {
      "name": "Subtitles",
      "description": "Read and replace the subtitle tracks of a recording (transcription, translation, dubbing), and read their saved versions."
    },
    {
      "name": "Templates",
      "description": "Saved sets of project settings: languages, preferences and translation settings. Members of your organization can read them; the owner or a manager changes them."
    },
    {
      "name": "Voices",
      "description": "The saved voices (\"My voices\") of your organization. Use a voice id to dub a speaker with it."
    },
    {
      "name": "Exports",
      "description": "Get the results as files: subtitles as text or documents, the source media, and the dubbed audio of a segment. A file export can run in the background; poll `GET …/exports/{exportId}` until it is `done`."
    },
    {
      "name": "Results",
      "description": "The saved results of a recording: summary, custom attributes, insights and safe communications. Order them with `summarize` and `transcribe`; they run in the background."
    },
    {
      "name": "Dubbing audio",
      "description": "Work on the audio of a dubbed language: bring the dubbing back in line with the translation, merge, split and change the speed of segments, replace the background audio, and read the state of those jobs."
    },
    {
      "name": "Credits",
      "description": "What an action would cost in credits, before you start it. Nothing is started and nothing is charged."
    },
    {
      "name": "Text to speech",
      "description": "Turn text into speech with a voice and an engine, and browse the voices: all, recommended and favorites. It does not need a project."
    },
    {
      "name": "Preferences",
      "description": "Your default settings for new projects: models, translation memory, machine translation profile and text-to-speech engine. A project can change them for itself."
    }
  ],
